Subject: [PATCH] Add third transfer pitfall (trailing-whitespace stripping)
 and tree-hash gate

The protocol patch itself arrived with whitespace-only lines stripped
(4 blank context lines and the '-- ' signature; evidence in 35d2120,
transfer/failed/). It still applied to the IDENTICAL tree
(220f8101d73bc884b2ee79a6b5763eea3ff7aa8f), because git treats an empty
line in a hunk as an empty context line. Lesson: the raw file sha256 is only
a difference detector; the authoritative gate for plain patches is git apply
--check + the post-am tree/blob hash, which are immune to whitespace stripping
and message edits.
